## Source-bounded blockers

1. `assign_open_front_boundary_authority()` requires an entry from `edge_matching_indices()` before classifying a boundary edge. That index intentionally contains only two-face interior edges, so a genuine one-face source boundary is rejected by construction.
2. Materialization counts an internal isolation seam as consumed only when it appears in cell-boundary `transitionSourceEdges`, then requires every retained region seam. The completed Review replaces that impossible witness with an exact reciprocal seam-transport certificate and validated local-sheet connectivity; unconditional marking or count/order/ID/proximity inference remains forbidden.
3. The two semantic-digest counterfactual tests live only in `tests/MilestoneGP27Tests.cpp`, which belongs to the disabled historical target. They are absent from the immutable package.
4. Several mandated quotient and retention counterfactuals have no independently discoverable default packaged test; retention has positive `true` evidence but no `false` counterpart.

## Reviewed remediation contract

- A genuine one-face source boundary is owned by non-empty canonical `sourceRouteTopology`; it has no interior matching index and therefore an empty `sourceRouteEdges` route.
- Do not expand `edge_matching_indices()`. Two-face ordinary, hard-rail, embedded-relief, and periodic transport retain strict interior index/provenance requirements.
- Every retained internal isolation seam receives one canonical reciprocal transport certificate. Materialization validates the certificate bijection and uses the certificates as each topology region's local-sheet connectivity graph.
- A seam is consumed only after its certificate participates in source-incidence, region/sheet, reciprocal-transport, cell/front/relation/quotient, lineage, hash, and diagnostics validation. Metadata-only or unconditional consumption remains forbidden.
- Every active counterfactual is compiled into the existing default producer-test executable; the broad historical target remains disabled.

